<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

    <PropertyGroup>
        <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
        <PackageId>X3Code.Repository</PackageId>
        <Product>X3Code.Repository</Product>
        <Title>X3-Code Repository</Title>
        <Description>Contains the unit of work repository pattern</Description>
        <PackageReleaseNotes>10.0.0: New version scheme - the major now tracks the .NET generation the package is built for (net10.0), the minor carries features and breaking changes, the patch carries fixes. All X3Code packages move to 10.0.0 together.
The package now ships its XML documentation, so consumers get IntelliSense. Added an MIT license expression, a README and a symbol package (snupkg) with SourceLink.
The README now documents IUnitOfWork, which groups the writes of several repositories into a single database transaction.
Entity Framework Core 10.0.3 -> 10.0.11.

1.10.3: Adds IUnitOfWork: a scope that puts the writes of several repositories into one database transaction
All asynchronous methods on IBaseRepository/BaseRepository now take a CancellationToken and pass it down into Entity Framework, matching what IUnitOfWork.BeginAsync already did. The parameter is optional, so existing call sites keep compiling.
BREAKING: DecimalExtension now lives in the X3Code.Repository.Extensions namespace instead of X3Code.Infrastructure.Extensions. Change the using in your DbContext. The type was previously compiled into both packages under the same name, which produced a CS0121 for anyone referencing X3Code.Repository and X3Code.Infrastructure together - and a consumer of this package should not have to write a using for a foreign package anyway.</PackageReleaseNotes>
    </PropertyGroup>

  <PropertyGroup>
    <!-- Haengt die gelinkte DecimalExtension.cs in den Namespace dieses Pakets, siehe Kommentar in der Datei. -->
    <DefineConstants>$(DefineConstants);X3CODE_REPOSITORY_LINK</DefineConstants>
  </PropertyGroup>

    <ItemGroup>
      <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore" />
      <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Relational" />
    </ItemGroup>

    <!-- Geteilte Quelldatei, bewusst statt eines ProjectReference. Siehe CLAUDE.md. -->
    <ItemGroup>
      <Compile Include="..\X3Code.Infrastructure\Extensions\DecimalExtension.cs">
        <Link>Extensions\DecimalExtension.cs</Link>
      </Compile>
    </ItemGroup>

</Project>
